  {
   "id": "matematicas-2019-reserva-1-4",
   "n": 4,
   "num": 4,
   "bloque": "Opción A",
   "puntos": "2,5",
   "enunciado": {
    "intro": "Considera el punto \\(A(2,1,0)\\) y los planos \\(\\pi_1\\equiv x+y+z=0\\) y \\(\\pi_2\\equiv x-y+z=0\\).",
    "apartados": [
     "(1,25 p.) Calcula la recta que pasa por \\(A\\) y es paralela a \\(\\pi_1\\) y a \\(\\pi_2\\).",
     "(1,25 p.) Calcula los puntos de la recta \\(s\\equiv\\dfrac{x-1}2=\\dfrac{y-2}3=\\dfrac z2\\) que equidistan de \\(\\pi_1\\) y \\(\\pi_2\\)."
    ]
   },
   "solucion": [
    {
     "titulo": "Apartado a",
     "html": "<div class='ex'><p>Una recta paralela a los dos planos tiene su director perpendicular a los dos vectores normales<i class='n' data-t='why'>Una recta es paralela a un plano si su director es perpendicular al vector normal del plano.</i>:</p>\\[\\vec d=\\vec n_1\\times\\vec n_2=\\begin{vmatrix}\\vec i&\\vec j&\\vec k\\\\1&1&1\\\\1&-1&1\\end{vmatrix}=(2,\\,0,\\,-2)\\parallel(1,0,-1)\\]<p>Pasa por \\(A(2,1,0)\\):</p><div class='f3d' data-f='{\"az\":15,\"el\":8,\"p\":[[\"poly\",[[-1.556,0.0,1.556],[1.838,0.0,-1.838],[0.859,1.96,-2.818],[-2.535,1.96,0.576]],\"#8b5cf6\",\"#7c3aed\"],[\"txt\",[0.859,1.96,-2.818],\"π₁\",\"#7c3aed\",4,0],[\"poly\",[[-1.556,0.0,1.556],[1.838,0.0,-1.838],[2.818,1.96,-0.859],[-0.576,1.96,2.535]],\"#fcd9a8\",\"#c2410c\"],[\"txt\",[2.818,1.96,-0.859],\"π₂\",\"#c2410c\",4,0],[\"line\",[0.4,1.0,1.6],[3.4,1.0,-1.4],\"#2563eb\",2.2,false],[\"txt\",[3.4,1.0,-1.4],\"t\",\"#2563eb\",6,0],[\"vec\",[2,1,0],[2.707,1.0,-0.707],\"#16a34a\",\"d\",4,-4],[\"pt\",[2,1,0],\"A\",7,-6]],\"ley\":[\"plano\",\"recta\",\"vector director\",\"puntos\"]}' style='overflow-x:auto'><svg viewBox='0 0 340 300' width='100%' style='max-width:440px' font-family='system-ui,sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='currentColor'><defs><marker id='m19r1a4n' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0 0L10 5L0 10z' fill='#dc2626'/></marker><marker id='m19r1a4d' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0 0L10 5L0 10z' fill='#16a34a'/></marker><marker id='m19r1a4g' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0 0L10 5L0 10z' fill='#64748b'/></marker><marker id='m19r1a4r' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0 0L10 5L0 10z' fill='#2563eb'/></marker></defs><polygon points='62.5,49.9 26.0,208.3 115.1,246.0 151.5,87.6' fill='#8b5cf6' fill-opacity='.26' stroke='#7c3aed' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='119.1' y='246.0' fill='#7c3aed' font-weight='700' font-style='italic'>π₁</text><polygon points='62.5,49.9 26.0,208.3 94.0,176.4 130.5,18.0' fill='#fcd9a8' fill-opacity='.26' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='98.0' y='176.4' fill='#c2410c' font-weight='700' font-style='italic'>π₂</text><line x1='81.5' y1='60.4' x2='49.3' y2='200.5' stroke='#2563eb' stroke-width='2.2'/><text x='55.3' y='200.5' fill='#2563eb' font-weight='700' font-style='italic'>t</text><line x1='64.3' y1='135.1' x2='56.8' y2='168.1' stroke='#16a34a' stroke-width='2.4' marker-end='url(#m19r1a4d)'/><text x='60.8' y='164.1' fill='#16a34a' font-weight='700'>d</text><circle cx='64.3' cy='135.1' r='3.8' fill='#e8487a'/><text x='71.3' y='129.1' font-weight='700'>A</text><line x1='24' y1='270' x2='19.9' y2='272.2' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='15.4' y='276.9' fill='#64748b' font-size='10'>x</text><line x1='24' y1='270' x2='39.5' y2='270.6' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='41.9' y='274.8' fill='#64748b' font-size='10'>y</text><line x1='24' y1='270' x2='24.0' y2='254.2' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='21.0' y='252.6' fill='#64748b' font-size='10'>z</text><g transform='translate(56.0,292)'><rect x='0' y='-8' width='12' height='9' fill='#8b5cf6' fill-opacity='.4' stroke='#7c3aed'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>plano</text></g><g transform='translate(106.5,292)'><line x1='0' y1='-4' x2='14' y2='-4' stroke='#2563eb' stroke-width='2'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>recta</text></g><g transform='translate(157.0,292)'><line x1='0' y1='-4' x2='14' y2='-4' stroke='#16a34a' stroke-width='2.4'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>vector director</text></g><g transform='translate(260.5,292)'><circle cx='6' cy='-4' r='3.8' fill='#e8487a'/><text x='18' y='0' font-size='10'>puntos</text></g></svg><p class='mut' style='font-size:.8rem;margin:.2rem 0;text-align:center'>Figura interactiva: arrástrala para girarla en 3D.</p></div><div class='res'>\\(r\\equiv\\begin{cases}x=2+t\\\\y=1\\\\z=-t\\end{cases}\\)</div></div>"
    },
    {
     "titulo": "Apartado b",
     "html": "<div class='ex'><p>Un punto genérico de \\(s\\) es \\(X(1+2t,\\,2+3t,\\,2t)\\). Como se trata de hallar los puntos que cumplen una condición de distancia, uso la fórmula de la distancia de un punto a un plano<i class='n' data-t='th'>\\(d(P,\\pi)=\\frac{|Ax_0+By_0+Cz_0+D|}{\\sqrt{A^2+B^2+C^2}}\\).</i>. Los dos normales tienen módulo \\(\\sqrt3\\):</p>\\[d(X,\\pi_1)=d(X,\\pi_2)\\iff\\frac{|x+y+z|}{\\sqrt3}=\\frac{|x-y+z|}{\\sqrt3}\\iff|3+7t|=|-1+t|\\]<p>• \\(3+7t=-1+t\\iff t=-\\dfrac23\\Rightarrow X_1\\left(-\\dfrac13,\\,0,\\,-\\dfrac43\\right)\\).</p><p>• \\(3+7t=1-t\\iff t=-\\dfrac14\\Rightarrow X_2\\left(\\dfrac12,\\,\\dfrac54,\\,-\\dfrac12\\right)\\).</p><div class='res'>\\(X_1\\left(-\\dfrac13,0,-\\dfrac43\\right)\\) y \\(X_2\\left(\\dfrac12,\\dfrac54,-\\dfrac12\\right)\\)</div><i class='n' data-t='tp'>Comprobación con \\(X_2\\): \\(x+y+z=\\frac54\\) y \\(x-y+z=-\\frac54\\): mismo valor absoluto ✓.</i></div>"
    }
   ],
   "clasificacion": [
    {
     "tema": "geom",
